 "q-31225" :question/id #uuid "ab3bcfde-03b1-5260-8f80-18e8461b51fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-31225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/assets/e8f5f537ad63035cac39ea672d4fd2bfff61d97590f79f83277e6654c9c05893.png)\n\nThe graph above shows $y={h}^{″}(x),$ where the function $h(x)$ is defined on $[-5,5].$ Find the intervals on which the function $h(x)$ is concave up." :question/worked-solution "A function $h(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${h}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={h}^{″}(x)$, we can see that ${h}^{″}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-3,0.75)$ and $(0.75,5).$ Therefore, the function $h(x)$ is concave up on the intervals $(-3,0.75)$ and $(0.75,5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31225/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1b60735-9dae-5c23-991d-0241c208b1b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "25ea632d-a340-5ca6-b886-7b32f73133ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2f39a81c-7ecc-555d-883b-6ea67e5464ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "adfc608a-b83c-551a-ada6-6e3a0a4499de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "fcbe04ef-8279-56b5-b622-faa830bb1c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "00b5eee6-2b71-5d97-98f4-e10289d41a0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "53b2e87f-9136-55d0-8549-3fbe6afd36d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79041/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-79041/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-79041/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-79041/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-79041/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-79041/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79041" :question/id #uuid "8bd473db-7b51-5cec-b077-da970bb7b859" :question/math-academy-id "q-79041" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-1,1)$\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,-1)$\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12x-4{x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12-12{x}^{2} \\\\  & =12(1-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =12(1+x)(1-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1+x)(1-x) & >0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-1) & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this inequality by considering the graph of $y=(x+1)(x-1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/assets/09b4b237ec87a63e6de47eea5ed9156febbed0271dd0688c0be1c22a62c50c4e.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that $(x+1)(x-1)<0$ when $-1<x<1.$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(-1,1).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $(x+1)(x-1)>0,$ which has the solutions $(-\\infty ,-1)$ and $(1,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c5e96422-26ae-5396-b76d-ff245e96bcfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "ed071224-8daa-5dbc-b675-93c3bf27608c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6646c1ae-dd3e-59d7-8786-2633e5de810b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343146/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-343146/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-343146/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4022d6aa-e7a1-5cc8-b441-dd8b1efe822f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cdef858-6874-5c3e-9c38-59e8a66a0ab3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343146/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-343146/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "54fddde1-00a5-5c23-9d33-26479c485ee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2538b3-2625-57b8-a435-029a36687462" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343146/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-343146/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-4/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0866cd13-4086-562d-ae6a-193aa22c57ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b3a484f-84d0-5670-9864-97137baeee92" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343146/field-4/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-343146/field-4/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343146" :question/id #uuid "6ce94e4f-6bff-561d-bee3-cf3e011e5b47" :question/math-academy-id "q-343146" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/assets/19d9904c5236534ee6b4f176d760268df397f644d4ea7016d1d35c4b5db6e413.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\nThe graph of the second derivative $y={g}^{″}(x)$ of the function $g(x)$ intersects the $x$-axis at the points $x=-4,$ $x=-2,$ $x=0,$ $x=2,$ and $x=4,$ as shown above. The intervals on which the function $g(x)$ is concave up are\n\n$(-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$),\\,(${{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$),\\,(${{field-4}}$,4).$" :question/worked-solution "A function $g(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${g}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={g}^{″}(x)$, we can see that ${g}^{″}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-4),$ $(-2,0),$ and $(2,4).$ \n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is concave up on the intervals \n\n$$\n(\\,-\\infty ,-4\\,),\\,(\\,-2,0\\,),\\,(\\,2,4\\,).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343146/field-1" "q-343146/field-2" "q-343146/field-3" "q-343146/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1b60735-9dae-5c23-991d-0241c208b1b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344876/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d9ea2f30-cd83-5d8a-b908-b17291f4f101" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344876/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4dc8f1b-3600-59ca-9f0e-bc7d6ed11f54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344876/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-344876/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344876/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0430e05f-f020-5ee7-b611-6f83ba763a7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344876/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a61a2655-b56d-5549-9963-28fa87d13bf0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344876/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e